A vulnerability disclosure policy should include following elements:
- vulnerability report contents;
- secure communication options as detailed in [PRE-5]
- publication;
- recognition.

A product shall be identifiable by providing at least the following information:
- manufacturer name;
- product name;
- (for hardware): any hardware product identifier, if applicable;
- (for software): any software product identifier, if applicable.

For each identified hardware component as per [PRE-8-RQ-01], the following information shall be recorded:
- hardware producer;
- component name;
- component identifier;
- if applicable, firmware version.

A security test and review plan shall consider at least the following aspects:
- product context;
- cybersecurity architecture and design;
- product cybersecurity requirements;
- risk assessment;
- test cases and test methodologies.

Security reviews shall consider at least the following sources:
- standards and publications describing the state-of-the-art in cybersecurity;
- changes in the threat landscape applicable to the product;
- vulnerabilities found in the product and its components;
- vulnerabilities found in similar products and their components; or
- information about the practical conditions of use as obtained by customer feedback, for example, due to support cases.

The publication shall contain at least, but not limited to, the following information to enable the target audience to decide if the vulnerabilities are relevant and how to remediate them:
- description of the vulnerability;
- vulnerability identifier;
- information allowing the identification of the affected product;
- potential impact of the vulnerability;
- severity of the vulnerability;
- detailed information on how to remediate the vulnerability;
- release date and update date.

The risk assessment is based on the products' context and the risk assessment results in an evaluation of identified risks.
The assessment of risks includes:
- an identification of the assets and cybersecurity objectives;
- an identification of the threats;
- an estimation of the risks;
- an evaluation of the risks.
